    heroSubhead: "Expert care for patients with more complex medical needs, with a focus on thorough evaluation, precision treatment, and long-term health planning. Your care is led directly by Dr. Andrew Hemmen, a board-certified internal medicine physician who has served New Mexico since 2008.",
    heroImage: {"src": "/images/dr-hemmen-imaging-review.jpg", "alt": "Dr. Andrew Hemmen reviewing imaging on a large-format display in a Body1MD exam room", "width": 800, "height": 579, "focus": "center 0%"},
    introHeading: "What Is Internal Medicine?",
    intro: ["Internal medicine is a specialty branch of medicine pertaining to the prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and management of diseases affecting adults over the age of 18. Doctors who practice internal medicine are known as internists and often serve as a patient's primary care provider. Internists may work together with other physicians to ensure patients are getting comprehensive care that transcends a specific symptom or health condition.","Dr. Andrew Hemmen earned his medical degree from St. George's University School of Medicine in 2003 and completed his Internal Medicine residency at Lenox Hill Hospital in New York in 2006. He has served New Mexico since 2008 and brings more than 20 years of experience caring for hospitalized patients, including serving as Chief Hospitalist during the opening of Presbyterian Rust Medical Center in 2011.","After years of treating people when they were sick enough to be in the hospital, Dr. Hemmen decided to practice medicine further upstream. Body1MD was built to give patients more time with their doctor, faster access, and a proactive plan designed to help keep preventable problems from becoming serious ones."],
    signsHeading: "An Internist May Be the Right Fit If You:",
    signsList: ["Are an adult looking for a physician to partner with on long-term health, prevention and screening","Live with more than one chronic condition, such as diabetes, high blood pressure, high cholesterol or heart disease","Take several medications and want one physician reviewing how they fit together","Have symptoms that cross body systems and have not been explained by looking at one organ at a time","See several specialists and want someone to put all the pieces of your health together","Want a physician who manages long-term disease and also treats sudden, acute illness"],
    bullets: ["Initial and follow-up visits designed to last up to an hour, so complex histories get the time they deserve","A head-to-toe review of your history, medications, symptoms and goals","Testing ordered when it will answer a real question or change your care","Imaging and results reviewed together on large-format displays in the exam room","Coordination with surgeons and other specialists when you need them","Direct access to Dr. Hemmen by phone and text between visits"],
