    approach: [{"title":"Thorough Evaluation","body":"We begin with a comprehensive consultation, looking at your health from head to toe, so we can fully understand you, your history, and your goals. Dr. Hemmen reviews your records, medications and prior results, examines you, and orders the testing that will actually answer the open questions.","iconPath":"M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2 M9 12h6m-6 4h6"},{"title":"Precision Treatment","body":"Internists do not treat one part of the body in isolation. Dr. Hemmen weighs how each condition and each medication affects the others, then builds a treatment plan that fits your physiology, your preferences and your daily life, and adjusts it as results come in.","iconPath":"M9.75 3.104v5.714a2.25 2.25 0 01-.659 1.591L5 14.5M9.75 3.104c-.251.023-.501.05-.75.082m.75-.082a24.301 24.301 0 014.5 0m0 0v5.714c0 .597.237 1.17.659 1.591L19.8 15.3M14.25 3.104c.251.023.501.05.75.082M19.8 15.3l-1.57.393A9.065 9.065 0 0112 15a9.065 9.065 0 00-6.23-.693L5 14.5m14.8.8l1.402 1.402c1.232 1.232.65 3.318-1.067 3.611A48.309 48.309 0 0112 21c-2.773 0-5.491-.235-8.135-.687-1.718-.293-2.3-2.379-1.067-3.61L5 14.5"},{"title":"Long-Term Health Planning","body":"Your health isn't a one-time visit, it's a continuous journey. Beyond managing today's problems, we plan for prevention, screening and the habits that keep preventable problems from becoming serious ones, and we revisit that plan as your needs change.","iconPath":"M16.023 9.348h4.992v-.001M2.985 19.644v-4.992m0 0h4.992m-4.993 0l3.181 3.183a8.25 8.25 0 0013.803-3.7M4.031 9.865a8.25 8.25 0 0113.803-3.7l3.181 3.182m0-4.991v4.99"}],
    benefits: [{"title":"A Physician Who Sees the Whole Picture","body":"It is common for patients to have a different doctor for different diseases or symptoms. Internal medicine physicians are the specialists who put all the pieces of your biological puzzle together, so you have one physician who understands how your conditions connect."},{"title":"Hospital-Tested Experience","body":"Dr. Hemmen spent more than 20 years caring for hospitalized patients, including serving as Chief Hospitalist during the opening of Presbyterian Rust Medical Center. That experience with serious illness now informs a practice built around prevention."},{"title":"Time to Think It Through","body":"Initial and follow-up visits are designed to last up to an hour, giving Dr. Hemmen the opportunity to understand your health, answer your questions, and develop a personalized action plan."},{"title":"Coordinated Specialist Care","body":"Internists know how to work together with surgeons and other specialists to coordinate your care. When you need a referral, Dr. Hemmen explains why and stays involved afterward."},{"title":"Timely Access","body":"With a deliberately limited patient panel, Body1MD offers same- or next-day appointments in most cases, and members have direct access to Dr. Hemmen by phone and text."},{"title":"No Insurance Hassles","body":"Body1MD operates outside of traditional insurance models. Membership is $100 per month under age 50 and $150 per month at 50 and older, month-to-month, so your visits are shaped by your needs rather than billing codes."}],
    timelineHeading: "What to Expect as a New Patient",
    timeline: [{"title":"Comprehensive Consultation","body":"Your first visit is designed to last up to an hour. Bring your medication list, recent records and test results, and the questions you most want answered. Dr. Hemmen reviews your history from head to toe and examines you."},{"title":"Testing and Results Review","body":"When testing is needed, Dr. Hemmen orders it and then reviews the results with you, often together on the exam room's large-format display, so you understand what the numbers mean."},{"title":"Your Personalized Plan","body":"Together you build a plan covering current conditions, medications, preventive screenings, and lifestyle steps such as nutrition and exercise."},{"title":"Ongoing Partnership","body":"Follow-up visits, direct phone and text access, and regular refinement of your plan keep you moving forward. If you need a specialist or hospital care, Dr. Hemmen helps coordinate it."}],
    extraSections: [{"heading":"Did You Know?","body":["Internal medicine physicians complete at least three years of residency training after medical school, focused on the diagnosis and treatment of diseases that affect adults. Not to be confused with interns, internists have a comprehensive understanding of the entire body and the systems inside it.","It is the internist's job to evaluate all of a patient's medical concerns and symptoms, not just those pertaining to a specific area of the body or medical specialty."]},{"heading":"Why Internal Medicine Fits Direct Primary Care","body":["Complex care takes time. In a rushed, insurance-driven appointment it is hard to untangle several conditions at once. Body1MD keeps a deliberately limited patient panel and visits designed to last up to an hour, so Dr. Hemmen can stay closely involved in each patient's care.","The membership is month-to-month with no annual contract, and there is no annual concierge retainer. You can request a visit online at body1md.com/book, with no account or login, or call (505) 645-5451 to get started."]}],
    faqs: [{"q":"Should I visit an internist?","a":"Everyone should have a primary care provider. If you are an adult age 18 or older, consider making an appointment with an internal medicine provider to discuss your current health and long-term wellness goals. If you are healthy, your internist will be your partner in maintaining your health, preventing illness, and screening for disease. If you are sick or experiencing symptoms, your internist will work to minimize your symptoms and restore your overall health."},{"q":"What types of conditions can I see an internal medicine physician for?","a":"Internists do not treat specific areas of the body; rather, they treat patients as a whole. They are equipped and trained to manage chronic disease, as well as treat sudden, acute illness. The internist understands both physical and mental health and can treat issues often managed by other specialists, such as reproductive, neurological, dermatological, ear, nose, and throat problems. Though patients are sometimes referred to other types of specialists, the internist serves as a first line of defense when issues arise."},{"q":"What is the benefit of seeing an internist?","a":"It is common for patients to have a different doctor for different diseases or symptoms. But internal medicine physicians are the specialists who put all the pieces of your biological puzzle together. They are lifetime care providers who do more than perform check-ups or write prescriptions, and they know how to work together with surgeons and other specialists to coordinate your care."},{"q":"Is internal medicine the same as family medicine?","a":"Both are primary care specialties. Family medicine physicians train to care for patients of all ages, including children. Internists focus on adults, with in-depth training in the diagnosis and management of adult disease, including complex and chronic conditions. Dr. Hemmen is board-certified in internal medicine."},{"q":"How does internal medicine work in a direct primary care membership?","a":"Body1MD is a direct primary care practice and does not bill insurance. The primary care membership is $100 per month under age 50 and $150 per month at age 50 and older, month-to-month, with no annual contract and no annual concierge retainer. Members get visits designed to last up to an hour, same- or next-day appointments in most cases, and direct access to Dr. Hemmen."}],
